:"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/HeavyLightDecomposition\/init(_:)-7w6b0","url":"\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/heavylightdecomposition\/init(_:)-7w6b0","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Decomposes an arborescence. O(n).","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Arborescence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Trees12ArborescenceV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">)","kind":"text"}]},"doc://TreeAlgorithms/documentation/TreeAlgorithms/HeavyLightDecomposition":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/treealgorithms\/heavylightdecomposition","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HeavyLightDecomposition"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The heavy–light decomposition of a rooted tree or arborescence: each vertex’s heavy child is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its child with the largest subtree (the first in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"children(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" order on a tie), and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"heavy edges form paths. Vertices get positions in a preorder that takes the heavy child first,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so each heavy path and each subtree is an interval of positions, and any path between two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices is at most 2⌊log₂ n⌋ + 1 intervals ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"segments(from:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":"), for path and subtree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queries over a structure indexed by position."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HeavyLightDecomposition"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"HeavyLightDecomposition","identifier":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms\/HeavyLightDecomposition"},"doc://TreeAlgorithms/documentation/TreeAlgorithms":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/treealgorithms","role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"TreeAlgorithms","identifier":"doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/documentation\/TreeAlgorithms"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Arborescence":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An arborescence: a directed tree whose edges all point away from its root, so every vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but the root has exactly one incoming edge, from its parent (NetworkX "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"is_arborescence"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Edmonds). A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the children, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the parent (zero or one), and each edge is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedEdge(from: parent, to: child)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/trees\/arborescence","title":"Arborescence","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Arborescence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}